{"id": "1b65771d-6d3e-4603-b5c5-b6803d31eeb6", "sessionId": "e09e7f99-3649-d72b-51ec-e48aa428a577", "turnId": "ad8fb115-2aec-4cca-873f-245f6e4885f7", "createdAt": 1789591139346, "updatedAt": 1789591140129, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "`RRFRanker` is the right way to do hybrid search when you want to **combine results from multiple retrieval methods** (e.g., lexical/BM25 and vector/semantic search) using **Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF)**. It requires **two or more pre-ranked result lists** (e.g., from a keyword search and a vector search) as input to perform the fusion.\n\n[Hybrid Search](https://docs.mistral.ai/studio/agents/introduction#hybrid-search)\n[Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF)](https://docs.mistral.ai/studio/agents/introduction#reciprocal-rank-fusion-rrf)"}], "source": null, "userDisplayContent": null}
